## Designer "Create Relationship" dialog: split into Label + ID fields

Context: the quick-create dialog shown when connecting two entities on the
Ontology Designer (D3 map) had a single "Relationship Name" field. Users
asked for separate editable Label and ID fields — cursor defaults to Label,
ID mirrors the Label live (camelCase) until edited directly, and ID must be
unique across the ontology or Create is blocked with an inline error.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js
   `showMapRelationshipDialog`: two fields (`mapRelationshipLabel`,
   `mapRelationshipName`). Label auto-focuses (via `shown.bs.modal`, since a
   synchronous `.focus()` right after `.show()` gets overridden by
   Bootstrap's own modal focus-trap). Typing in Label mirrors into ID via
   `columnToCamelCase()` until the user edits the ID field directly
   (`idManuallyEdited` flag, set only by a real `input` event on the ID
   field — programmatic mirroring doesn't trigger it). `validateName()`
   checks the ID is non-empty and not already used by any property in
   `OntologyState.config.properties` (Bootstrap `is-invalid` +
   `invalid-feedback`), blocking the Create button on failure. Resolves
   `{ name, label }` instead of a bare string.
   `createRelationshipFromMap` updated for the new `{ name, label }` shape
   and its duplicate check widened from domain+range-scoped to global by
   `name` (properties are looked up by name alone everywhere else in the
   app, e.g. `editPropertyByName`, so scoping this check to domain+range was
   a latent bug — two properties sharing a name but different domain/range
   would have broken those lookups).
2. tests/units/front/test_map_relationship_dialog.py
   Contract tests: both fields present, Label autofocus wiring (`shown.bs.modal`),
   ID mirroring + manual-edit override, uniqueness validation blocking
   Create, `{name, label}` resolve shape, and the widened global uniqueness
   check + label wiring in `createRelationshipFromMap`.

