## Simplify navbar breadcrumb: main menu + sub menu only

Context: the top-right breadcrumb showed "Registry > <DomainName> > <MainMenu>
> <SubMenu>" for Ontology/Mapping/Domain/Knowledge Graph pages. Users asked
to drop the Registry and Domain-name ancestor crumbs entirely and show only
the current main menu (Ontology, Mapping, etc.) and the sub menu (sidebar
section) selected within it.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/breadcrumb.js
   `_buildCrumbs()` no longer walks a `_HIERARCHY` array to push ancestor
   "Registry" / domain-name crumbs — it always returns just the single
   matched main-menu entry from `_ROUTE_MAP`; `_updateSection()` (unchanged)
   still appends the active sidebar section as the second/last crumb.
   Removed the now-unused `_HIERARCHY` constant and `_getDomainName()`
   helper. `init()`'s hide guard changed from `crumbs.length <= 1` (hid the
   breadcrumb whenever there were no ancestors to show) to
   `crumbs.length === 0` (hides only when the current path isn't a
   recognized main menu at all).
2. tests/units/front/test_breadcrumb.py
   Contract tests: no Registry/ancestor logic in `_buildCrumbs`, removed
   `_HIERARCHY`/`_getDomainName`/`currentDomainName` references, single-crumb
   return shape, and the relaxed hide guard.

